  "notes": "The English rock producer who brought \"a British pop sensibility\" into Nashville-adjacent Americana — the outsider entry on this board, and included because \"the 'rehearsed, organic, pop-tidied' method is a distinct point on this board.\" His stated contribution is bringing \"some pop elements to the music,\" which the entry translates as \"pop turnarounds (ii–V–I, IV–I/3–V) and chromatic pre-chorus motion inside otherwise-roots material,\" so ii–V–I is a family and a small chromatic weight sits in the scales. Drums are \"explicitly 'organic,' preferring live studio recording over layered track assembly — bands cut together, 2&4, with real room. Model low overdub count and pattern consistency,\" which is a played humanize with an unusually low fill count and a narrow density range: consistency is the parameter. The most transferable fact is his process discipline and it lands squarely on the arrangement block: \"artists must arrive fully rehearsed and ready, and he worked structured nine-hour days ending by 8pm rather than late-night sessions. That produces tight, pre-arranged records — **model fixed section lengths and no in-studio restructuring**,\" so every `sectionBars` value here is a scalar rather than a range and `switchUpProb` sits at the floor — the only model in this section authored that way. He also worked as an arranger, \"so string and harmony-vocal arrangements are written rather than improvised,\" which is the counter's sustained-pad weighting. `relatedGenres` is held to the two lanes the entry states — the country-pop board he is placed on and the \"British pop sensibility\" he is here for; the entry documents a straight 2&4 and never a shuffle, and this name is not on the section's own `country-shuffle` flag list, so that id is not claimed. ⚠ Confidence is medium and the research says why: \"philosophy and process documented; country-specific technique not [LOW-CONF].\" ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the velocity tiers, the perc set and the counter ratio.",
